# Git commit messages

- Format: `type(scope): concise description` (Conventional Commits, English, < 120 chars).
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`.
- Scope is the targeted package (`core`, `browser`, etc.).
- Description: imperative, lowercase, no period, no body. Name the file-level change, not vague words (`update`, `changes`, `improvements`, `misc`).
- Add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry for new or modified files unless the change is trivial. Do not duplicate existing entries.

Examples: `feat(core): add typed document builder`, `fix(browser): prevent duplicate font registration`
